oric":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{R}{R}","name":"Sowing Salt","oracle_id":"131d2b70-959d-4814-b0c8-38031f141718","oracle_text":"Exile target nonbasic land. Search its controller's graveyard, hand, and library for all cards with the same name as that land and exile them. Then that player shuffles.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2005-02-04","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Reach","Morph"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{G}{G}","name":"Spitting Gourna","oracle_id":"413e8f01-4ee0-48df-8647-c614db38681e","oracle_text":"Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\nMorph {4}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)","power":"3","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2002-10-07","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature — Beast"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{G}{G}","name":"Splinter","oracle_id":"90f01e9f-68f1-4e41-97dc-8de990a91504","oracle_text":"Exile target artifact. Search its controller's graveyard, hand, and library for all cards with the same name as that artifact and exile them. Then that player shuffles.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2005-02-04","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Does not exile other cards of the same name that are on the battlefield. Just from the graveyard, hand, and library.","oracle_id":"131d2b70-959d-4814-b0c8-38031f141718","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copies must be found if they are in publicly viewable zones. Finding copies while searching private zones is optional.","oracle_id":"131d2b70-959d-4814-b0c8-38031f141718","published_at":"2005-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that instruct you to reveal or look at cards from the top of you library will still work. Only effects that use the word \"search\" are affected.","oracle_id":"5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect says \"Search your library . . . then shuffle your library,\" you shuffle you libraries even though you can't search.","oracle_id":"5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect says \"You may search your library . . . If you do, shuffle your library\" or \"You may search your library . . . then shuffle your library,\" you can't choose to search, so you won't shuffle.","oracle_id":"5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The only difference between a colored artifact and a colorless artifact is, obviously, its color. Unlike most artifacts, a colored artifact requires colored mana to cast. Also unlike most artifacts, a colored artifact has a color in all zones. It will interact with cards that care about color. Other than that, a colored artifact behaves just like any other artifact. It will interact as normal with any card that cares about artifacts, such as Shatter or Arcbound Ravager.","oracle_id":"5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Does not exile other cards of the same name that are on the battlefield. Just from the graveyard, hand, and library.","oracle_id":"782ff740-ff43-4c07-af0b-433cb9770661","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a copy card is targeted by this effect, you get to look for another copy of the card it is copying. This is because a copy card actually takes on the name and initial characteristics of what it copies.","oracle_id":"782ff740-ff43-4c07-af0b-433cb9770661","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Use the name of the card as it leaves the battlefield.","oracle_id":"782ff740-ff43-4c07-af0b-433cb9770661","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you manage to turn a land (such as a Forest or Stalking Stones) into a creature, you can indeed use this effect on that basic land type. Eradicate’s exile effect only looks for cards by name, not type.","oracle_id":"782ff740-ff43-4c07-af0b-433cb9770661","published_at":"2005-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copies must be found if they are in publicly viewable zones. Finding copies while searching private zones is optional.","oracle_id":"782ff740-ff43-4c07-af0b-433cb9770661","published_at":"2005-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A face-down creature has no name, so no card can possibly share a name with it (not even other cards with no name). If you Eradicate a face-down creature you will still search its controller’s library, but you won’t be able to exile any cards from that library.","oracle_id":"782ff740-ff43-4c07-af0b-433cb9770661","published_at":"2012-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Does not exile other cards of the same name that are on the battlefield. Just from the graveyard, hand, and library.","oracle_id":"90f01e9f-68f1-4e41-97dc-8de990a91504","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Splinter can target and exile cards that aren’t always artifacts, but are artifacts when Splinter is cast and resolves (such as an animated Stalking Stones). Splinter’s exile effect only looks for cards by name, not type.","oracle_id":"90f01e9f-68f1-4e41-97dc-8de990a91504","published_at":"2005-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copies must be found if they are in publicly viewable zones. Finding copies while searching private zones is optional.","oracle_id":"90f01e9f-68f1-4e41-97dc-8de990a91504","published_at":"2005-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Act of Treason can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple effects modify your hand size, apply them in timestamp order. For example, if you put Null Profusion (an enchantment that says your maximum hand size is two) onto the battlefield and then put Reliquary Tower onto the battlefield, you'll have no maximum hand size. However, if those permanents enter in the opposite order, your maximum hand size would be two.","oracle_id":"c23e5b80-08d2-4e24-9908-fe2aa4f30f6f","published_at":"2009-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Does not exile other cards of the same name that are on the battlefield. Just from the graveyard, hand, and library.","oracle_id":"f18622da-81f3-4854-a1bb-8d658751d8db","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Scour can target and exile cards that aren’t always enchantments, but are enchantments when Scour is cast and resolves (such as creatures turned into enchantments by Soul Sculptor). Scour’s exile effect only looks for cards by name, not type.","oracle_id":"f18622da-81f3-4854-a1bb-8d658751d8db","published_at":"2005-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copies must be found if they are in publicly viewable zones. Finding copies while searching private zones is optional.","oracle_id":"f18622da-81f3-4854-a1bb-8d658751d8db","published_at":"2005-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Becoming an artifact doesn't change what color(s) a permanent is.","oracle_id":"f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may target any permanent with the ability, including an artifact.","oracle_id":"f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
